Linux files used by the illumos DRM port

Upstream: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/stable/linux.git
Version: v7.2
Commit: 8d3ae59288f1e7d58d76558a6ee96d533bc5019f

This is the pristine upstream subset, imported on linux-pristine; port changes
are separate commits on the main integration line. The initial list is the
textually normalized union of the i915 display, i915 headless and drm_kms
linux-inputs.txt lists built at illumos-drm e101f9814da43756bc7f13f02ae6020f05e7d069,
with .illumos/mit-include paths mapped to include/, the six GPL originals
excluded, and fourteen build-script inputs added (five fetch-time header copies
and nine licence-generation fallback headers). SOURCES records each upstream
path, its pristine SHA-256 and its licence class, separated by tabs. All 847
upstream files passed drivers/i915/check-licences.py: SPDX MIT or a dual licence
offering MIT, or an MIT/HPND permission notice; every original notice is kept.

.gitattributes disables Git text conversion throughout this directory so the
upstream and patched bytes remain exact regardless of clone configuration.

The four tracepoint headers are committed MIT outputs of
 drivers/i915/illumos/gen-trace-stubs.py; intel_ips.h and
 drm_dp_mst_topology_internal.h are MIT replacements from this repository.
Their six GPL originals are never imported. Today fetch-and-patch.sh generates
the four trace stubs at fetch time; in the vendored model they are committed
stand-ins and gen-trace-stubs.py is a maintainer tool for pin updates. This
import does not change the existing fetch script or build path.

The maintainer generators drivers/i915/config/gen-config.py and
 drivers/i915/illumos/gen-nodisplay.py need a full upstream checkout at the pinned
commit, passed as their tree argument. They run only when the pin or the
configuration changes; their outputs are committed and a normal build does not
run either generator.

Verify from the repository root, supplying a prepared fetch-and-patch tree:
  sh usr/src/contrib/linux/verify-vendored.sh -p /path/to/full/linux /path/to/prepared/linux
Repeat -i /path/to/linux-inputs.txt for each build input list. The optional -p
checks SOURCES against Git objects of the full upstream checkout, independently
of linux-pristine; every vendored source is compared with the prepared tree and
checked by the existing Python licence gate. The directory walk excludes only
.gitattributes, SOURCES, README and verify-vendored.sh.

To update, regenerate the build input lists and SOURCES for the new pin, import
pristine MIT-compatible bytes on linux-pristine, merge it into the integration
branch, and review conflicts with the port commits. Regenerate the stand-ins
from the new pin and repeat the byte comparisons and licence gate on illumos.
